- Form 1098‑E for student loan interest (from FedLoan).
- Records to prove home office size (sketch or floor plan showing 100 sq ft out of 690 sq ft) and rent receipts, utility bills, internet bills, repairs, etc., if you use the actual method.
- Receipts/invoices for the $780 business expenses (if they are for the self‑employment activity).
- Any 1099‑NEC or client invoices showing the $8,900.

11) State return (California)
- File CA Form 540. California generally follows federal reporting of business income and student loan interest treatment is typically similar, but there are differences in some itemized/adjustment rules — if you want, I can pull CA specifics or walk through your CA return after confirming spouse income and any CA adjustments.

12) Other considerations
- Because you had self‑employment income, ensure enough tax was withheld or make estimated tax payments to avoid underpayment penalties. If you expect similar or larger self‑employment income next year, consider making quarterly estimated payments or increasing W‑2 withholding.
- If your spouse also has income or other deductions/credits, those will affect AGI and whether student‑loan interest phases out; please tell me spouse income if you want a more precise phaseout check.

Quick checklist of next steps I can help with
